{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And they shall answer and say.</b> It refers to the elders, which follows from the preceding." "<b>Our hands did not spill.</b> It is written with a heh to teach that a host owes his guest five things: food, drink, escort, lodging, and a gift — a large item or a small one. And did it cross our minds that the elders of Israel, a court, spill blood? Rather, he did not come into our hands and we let him go without provisions. This is Rashi's explanation. And that is <b>our hands did not spill</b> — that is, he needed provisions and did not have them, and one saw a man carrying provisions and came to snatch them from him because of the force of his hunger, and this one stood against him and killed him." "<b>And our eyes did not see.</b> We did not see him and let him go without escort — this is Rashi's explanation; a group to go with him, as it is taught, and so Rashi explained in Sotah. Another interpretation: <b>and our eyes did not see</b> — from here, one who escorts his fellow must stand in his place until he disappears from his eyes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:36.529508282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}